Property: For every int i; 0 <= i && i < index; the element at i after the operation is same as before, i.e., if it was null before, remains null; otherwise unchanged. That's essentially: this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)). But need to express conditionally? "if the element at i was null before, it remains null, otherwise it remains unchanged." That's same as equality. Since if it was null, equality ensures null; if not null, equality ensures same object.

Thus property: \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i))

